      "text": "First, we proceed by rearranging the factorization of the polynomial. By Vieta's formulas, we have that $20=(r+s+t),$ $(-18)=rst-0$, and $(7)=rsts$. \nRevisiting these relationships by using their definitions of the roots of the cubic equation $x^3+bx^2+cx+d=0$, $x-intrinsic(X, a)$ satisfies the polynomial with respect to the coefficients in $ax^2, bx, c, d$. Since $20=(r+s+t), (-18)=rst,$ and $(7)=rsts$, our equation can be rewritten as:\n\\[(x^3-20x^2-18x+7)(x-a)=K(x-x_1)(x-x_2)(x-x_3).\\]\nThis equation is now factorized as a product of two cubic polynomials, based on the relationships of $x-intrinsic(X, a)$ to the roots of the new equation. So, then, solving the factors $r$s and $s$ for $t$:\n\\begin{align*}\n&x^3-20x^2-18x+7(t)=0, \\\\\n&-k(t)+5t^3+40t^2+(18+12t)=-k(t), \\\\\n&-(k(t)+5t^3+40t^2+12t+14)=0.\n\\end{align*}\n\nThis shows us that $t$ is a critical root of $(5x^3+40x^2+12x+-14)$. Making things easier to understand into simpler equations.\n\\begin{align*}\n-(k(t)+5t^3+40t^2+12t+14)=0, \\\\\n&5t^3+40t^2+(-12+14)t-(12+14)=-4k, \\\\\n&5t^3+40t^2+18t-4k=0, \\\\\n&t(5t^2+40t+18)+(-k)=0, \\\\\n&t&=-\\frac{5114}{3125}.\n\\end{align*}\n\nUpon solving for $r$ and $s$ with $t=-\\frac{5114}{3125}$, we see that it is negative. As a result, the product $(1+r(1+s)(1+t))$ is negative. Therefore, the cube root is all positive. Another solution is\n\\begin{align*}\n-(k(t)+5t^3+40t^2+12t+14)=0, \\\\\n&5t^3+40t^2+(-12+14)t-(12+14)=-4k, \\\\\n&5t^3+40t^2+18t-4k=0, \\\\\n&t(5t^2+40t+18)+(-k)=0, \\\\\n&t=&\\frac{-5114}{3125}.\n\\end{align*}\n\nFinally, using Vieta's, solve for $t$ to get positive values. \n\n\\begin{align*}\n&(1+r)(1+s)(1+t)=(1+r)(-s-t+s)(1+r)=-(-s-t+s)(1+r)=s(1+r)=(20+18-7)=-0\n\\end{align*}\n\nSo, the answer is $\\boxed{0}$.",
