      "text": "To find the value of \\((1 + r)(1 + s)(1 + t)\\) for the roots \\(r, s, t\\) of the polynomial \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\\), we can use the relationships involving sums and products of roots.\n\nGiven the polynomial:\n\\[\nx^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\n\\]\n\nBy Vieta's formulas, we know:\n1. \\(r + s + t = 20\\) (sum of the roots)\n2. \\(rs + st + tr = 18\\) (sum of the products of the roots taken two at a time)\n3. \\(rst = 7\\) (product of the roots)\n\nWe need to compute \\((1 + r)(1 + s)(1 + t)\\).\n\nFirst, let’s express \\((1 + r)(1 + s)(1 + t)\\) in a different form:\n\\[\n(1 + r)(1 + s)(1 + t) = 1 + r + s + t + rs + st + tr + rst\n\\]\n\nNow substituting the known values from Vieta's formulas:\n\\[\n1 + r + s + t + rs + st + tr + rst = 1 + 20 + 18 + 7\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the right-hand side:\n\\[\n1 + 20 + 18 + 7 = 46\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\((1 + r)(1 + s)(1 + t)\\) is \\(\\boxed{46}\\).\n\nLet's verify our reasoning using Python code for accuracy.\n```python\n# Given values from Vieta's formulas\r\nsum_of_roots = 20\r\nsum_of_products_roots_together = 18\r\nproduct_of_roots = 7\r\n\r\n# Calculate the required expression\r\nresult = 1 + sum_of_roots + sum_of_products_roots_together + product_of_roots\r\nprint(result)\n```",
