      "text": "To find the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\) where \\(r, s, t\\) are the roots of the polynomial \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\\), we can use Vieta's formulas and some algebraic manipulation.\n\nFirst, by Vieta's formulas, for the polynomial \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\\), the sum of the roots taken one at a time (i.e., \\(r + s + t\\)) is:\n\\[\nr + s + t = 20.\n\\]\nThe sum of the product of the roots taken two at a time (i.e., \\(rs + rt + st\\)) is:\n\\[\nrs + rt + st = 18.\n\\]\nThe product of the roots \\(rst\\) is:\n\\[\nrst = 7.\n\\]\n\nWe need to find the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\). Expanding this expression, we get:\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + (r+s+t) + (rs + rt + st) + rst.\n\\]\nSubstituting the values from Vieta's formulas, we have:\n\\[\n1 + (r + s + t) + (rs + rt + st) + rst = 1 + 20 + 18 + 7.\n\\]\nSimplifying the right-hand side, we get:\n\\[\n1 + 20 + 18 + 7 = 46.\n\\]\nTherefore, the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\) is \\(\\boxed{46}\\).",
