      "text": "By Vieta's formulas, we know that\n\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Sum of the roots} &= r + s + t = 20, \\\\\n\\text{Sum of the roots taken two at a time} &= rs + rt + st = 18, \\text{ and}\\\\\n\\text{Product of the roots} &= rst = 7.\n\\end{align*}\nLet $a = 1 + r, b = 1 + s, c = 1 + t$. We can rewrite the product of three factors of $x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7$ as $(1 + r)(1 + s)(1 + t) = 1 + rs + rt + st + rst + r + s + t.$\nBy Vieta's formulas, we have $rs + rt + st = 18$ and $rst = 7.$ Therefore,\n\\begin{align*}\n1 + rs + rt + st + rst + r + s + t &= 1 + 18 + 7 + 20 = \\boxed{46}.\n\\end{align*}\nThe answer is: 46",
